// Permit reading stock info only for AMZN. The tool's `stock` argument is
// one of its inputs, so in the Drupe schema it
// lands at `context.input.stock` — meaning a plain Cedar `when` clause validates
// against it. A complete rule, with an @id.
//
@id("get_amzn_stock_info")
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"GetStockInfo",
    resource
)
when { context.input.stock == "AMZN" };
